@OpenAI solved a problem mathematicians have wrestled with for a quarter century.

@GoogleDeepMind mapped every possible mutation hiding in our genes. These are awe-inspiring feats of the machines.

In my latest piece for @time, I write about why, even as we marvel at AI’s capacity, we shouldn’t lose sight of something irreplaceable: human-generated awe.

Dacher Keltner, professor of psychology at the @ucberkeleyofficial, looked at 2,600 stories of awe across 26 countries. He found that what most commonly led people to feel awe wasn’t nature, or spirituality, or technology — it was watching ot…

Please don’t talk to me about balance! We can’t do it all or have it all, ALL the time—and that’s perfectly okay. It’s about accepting the inevitable tradeoffs, doing what you can, when you can and embracing the idea that sometimes “balance” may not exist.

